Readout
- Q4 and the 4x4 grid pass the median triple test: compatible sidecar
  hyperplanes give unique three-route consensus states.
- C6 is bipartite and small but fails medianity by triples with no
  candidate center; even-cycle structure is not enough.
- The Desargues graph is cubic, bipartite, girth 6, and has many median
  failures.  As an LRC analogy it is a compact incidence/duality warning,
  not a proof carrier by itself.
